    <td  bgcolor="#c0c0c0" width="100%" valign="top"><tt><font color="#000000">
Author:&nbsp;<a href="/showmember.php?name=Clunch">Clunch</a>&nbsp;(---.proxy.aol.com)<br>
Date:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;03-27-01 14:57<br>
<br><HTML>For those of you who have been away there have been some recent developements in the guild. Breakex and Gustave were removed from the guild. Taking Zorow and Woodlife with them. Xeritukrush quit because of the problems we were having during this time.<br>
I like to think we enjoy a certain amount of freedom in this guild. Nothing is ever mandatory. And the last thing i would want to do is tell someone how they can play this game. That being said with that freedom there will always be people there to abuse it. <br>
Noone regrets more the recent events than i do. And as a matter of fact I liked Breakex and would never voted him out, EXCEPT for the fact that i cast my vote as a representative of the guild. During the 3 days this was going on I did not receive a single tell telling me that 'break and gus are cool and if they leave im leaving'. I did howerver recieve several (more than 10) tells telling me that something had to be done.<br>
For those of you who dont know the story here it is:<br>
Breakex and Gustave had been dominating guild speak for about a week with there playful argument that they were having.This is very much allowed as this is the peoples guild to be used however the individual wishes. I would think that everyone would have enough consideration for there guild mates that I could make a statement like that without someone taking advantage. However, when a guild mate asked you to stop you should give there fellings some consideration. Instead Brteakex and Gustave spent the next three days insulting everyone within reach and TRYING there hardest to make sure that they would annoy EVERYONE in the guild especially the individual who had the gall to ask them to be quiet for a little while. Any attempt to talk to them peacefully only seemed to fan the flames. They had made several staements that this was a little, stupid, worthless, you name it guild and that they were leaving. They only seemed to be sticking around to ruin as many peoples day as possible. It took about 15 minutes to get the officers together fofr a unanymous vote that they be removed immediatly. The next day Gustave got on as his alt that I personally didnt know about and continued the process forcing Xeritukruch to quit before i could boot him.<br>
I am sorry to the rest of the guld for all the disruption this has caused hopefully now we can move on.</HTML></font></tt><p>
